if you've changed your playstation plus  subscription to take advantage of its  different tiers but are overwhelmed with  what to play next have no fear here's a  rundown of the best games to play on  playstation plus for august 2022  let's kick off with the free playstation  plus monthly games for august then which  you can download and play if you have a  playstation plus essential extra or  premium subscription spoiler alert this  is going to be a very yakuza heavy video  and the first free game on the list is  yakuza like a dragon for playstation 4  and playstation 5. yakuza like a dragon  has you play as ichiban kasiga a  low-ranking member of a yakuza crime  family who takes the fall for a murder  someone else committed only to be cast  aside by the patriarch of his family and  left for dead abandoned and betrayed by  his family ichiban gets a questionable  haircut and creates a new family of  misfits who inadvertently involve  themselves in risky yakuza politics  dangerous turf wars and delightful  confectionary stores while the other  yakuza games are button-mashing brawlers  like a dragon is turn-based with the  vivid imaginations of your party members  adding a little magic to the everyday  weapons you find lying around the  bustling streets of ijincho and if you  get fed up with your current moveset a  new one is just a job change away make  sure to grab yakuza like a dragon before  september 6th  rise and grind baby your next free game  for august is tony hawk's pro skater 1 2  for ps4 and ps5 the 2020 remake of two  of the most iconic playstation 1 games  is fantastic and we here at gamespot  gave it a 9 out of 10 in our review the  game was remade from the ground up with  environments receiving a fresh lick of  paint the original 21 skateboarders have  been aged up to their current age and a  number of new faces have also been added  to the roster the soundtrack is a mix of  songs from the original games and 37 new  tracks and before you ask yes superman  by goldfinger is still on there tony  hawk's pro skater feels as fun to play  now as it did back in 1999 so you'll be  pulling off wild high-flying combos in  no time  if you're in the mood for a puzzle  platformer that'll creep you out as much  as entertain you then little nightmares  is the game for you and it rounds off  the monthly august games for ps plus as  six you need to escape the more a  terrifying underwater resort that's  filled with monsters who are on the hunt  for fresh meat it's a relatively  straightforward platformer that you'll  likely finish in a couple of sittings  but it's a creepy trip that'll keep you  entertained throughout its run time  i wasn't joking when i said this would  be a yakuza heavy episode because eight  yes you heard me right eight yakuza  games are coming to playstation plus  this year meaning you'll be able to play  all of kazuma kiryu's story in one place  i already mentioned that yakuza like a  dragon will be one of august's monthly  games and the rest are coming to the  game catalog which you can access if  you're a playstation plus extra or  premium member while you don't need to  have played the other yakuza games to  enjoy or understand like a dragon they  certainly are complementary the yakuza  series is having a real moment lately  and thanks to its recent surge in  popularity more and more people are  getting to enjoy the thrills zany side  missions melodrama fisty cuffs and  karaoke that the series offers if you're  worried about being overwhelmed by too  much yakuza have no fear the games are  coming in two separate drops yakuza 0  kiwami and kiwami 2 will all be joining  the game catalogue in august along with  like a dragon yakuza 0 is the canonical  start of the series telling the story of  the early days of hero kazuma kiryu and  how he meets goro majima in 1980's  kamarocho japan it's followed by kiwami  and kiwami 2. remakes of yakuza 1 and 2  but with a new engine extra story  cutscenes and gameplay elements like the  fan favorite magima everywhere mechanic  i'm not going to delve too deeply into  spoiler territory but the rest of  kiryu's saga yakuza 3 remastered 4  remastered 5 remastered and 6 the song  of life will be added to the service at  a later date and they are well worth  playing there's a lot of yakuza on  playstation plus this year and honestly  i'm excited for you if you decide to get  into this series now it's one of my  favorites and there's no better time to  dive in  for extra and premium subscribers july's  game catalog titles dropped a couple of  weeks ago so here's a quick round up in  case there are any that you missed first  up stray if you've been on the internet  over the past month it's been impossible  to miss clips of the adorable cat that's  the star of stray and the real-life cats  that have also been enraptured by the  game you're in the shoes or should i say  pause of a cat separated from its sweet  cat family and dropped into a  dilapidated run-down city slum along  with your drone friend b12 and the  robots who inhabit the slums you explore  the city and try to find your way back  out by solving various puzzles and  platforming around the buildings there's  also a dedicated meow button so what  more could you ask for it's available on  both ps4 and ps5  also available is final fantasy 7 remake  integrated for playstation 5 the  upgraded version of final fantasy vii  remake which stunned players when it  launched in 2020. at gamespot we gave  final fantasy 7 remake a rare 10 out of  10 and integrate packages the base game  with a bunch of extra features including  improved textures graphics and  performance mode so you can choose what  to prioritize an in-depth photo mode and  dual sense integration so you can feel  every strike of that giant buster sword  integrate also includes a new episode of  the story intermission where you can  play as the cutest ninja around yuffie  if you're waiting for final fantasy 7  remake part 2 or want to experience the  story for the first time integrate is  the perfect way to do both  if the recent news of marvel's phase 5  has you hyped give marvel's avengers a  go on playstation in single player you  can play as some of the earth's  mightiest heroes as they battle evil  criminal organization aim and in  multiplayer you can level your  characters and take them online new  heroes like the mighty thor and black  panther have been added since launch  with more reportedly on the way the  game's multiplayer can certainly be a  bit of a grind but it's still enjoyable  with some pals and the single player is  a fun snappy story about heroes who have  lost confidence in themselves and the  journey to reuniting them as a team  if you fancy digging into some history  and making it your playground try some  assassins creed on for size a number of  ubisoft's flagship games are in the game  catalog including the ezio collection  rogue remastered and my personal  favorite assassin's creed iv black flag  where you can take to the high seas as  pirate edward kenway so if you're  waiting for the next mainline  installment of assassin's creed well  there are hundreds of hours of games  here for you  and finally a pick from the classics  catalogue which is available to premium  subscribers if you missed tokyo jungle  when it originally launched on  playstation 3 you can find it here tokyo  jungle is a throwback to classic easy to  pick up and hard to put down gameplay  with a quirky and brutal twist humankind  has gone nature has reclaimed the land  and all the animals are so so vicious  you can control everything from a tiny  little pomeranian to a majestic lion and  your goal is simply to survive it's kill  or be killed out there on the streets of  tokyo so that cute pomeranian has to be  bloodthirsty to live another day yes  tokyo jungle is brutal but it's also  very funny and a wonderful little gem  that would otherwise be lost to time so  give it a try if you've got premium  those are our picks for games to play on  playstation plus this month there are  hundreds of games on the service and the  catalogs are constantly changing so make  sure to subscribe to find the best games  to play to get the most out of your  subscription let me know what you'll be  playing in the comments below or  highlight some games you think deserve  more love i'm on twitter at lucy james  games and i'll see you next time  [Music]  you
 

